    "description": "- Development of a dental simulator (OpenGL, C++, Qt) \nbased on the volumetric model studied in my thesis: refined the contact and drilling models, improved the force feedback quality and precision and system calibration.\n  The system uses a real jaw model (mounted on a usb joystick) and a haptik device (Sensable or Haption).\n  10 systems installed in Switzerland and Netherlands.\n- Computed Tomography software DigiCT:\nbibliographic research, development (OpenGL, C++, Qt) and support. I made a lot of dataset reconstructions (pre-sale). Installation and customer training, sometimes in solo, at various location both in France and  internationally (Hannover, Zagreb, Houston, Minneapolis).\n  Development of an acquisition software to upgrade a 2D radiographic system into a 3D tomograph (camera and rotating plate control).",
